"AFS\",\"value\":\"stainless steel\"}, ...]},\n      {\"attribute\": \"load_cell_connection\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"values\": [{\"model\":\"AFS\",\"value\":\"4-wire\"}, ...]},\n      {\"attribute\": \"series\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"values\": [...]}\n    ],\n    \"config_level\": [\n      {\"attribute\": \"nh_marked_load_cell_permissible\", \"axis\": \"load cell marking / instrument humidity testing\", \"values\": [{\"condition\": \"NH-marked load cell\", \"value\": \"allowed only with R76 humidity testing\", \"unit_symbol\": null}]}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"test_reports\": [\n    {\"id\": \"P00917\", \"pages\": 13, \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"}\n  ],\n  \"recommendation\": {\n    \"id\": \"R76\",\n    \"edition\": 2006,\n    \"accuracy_classes\": [\"III\", \"IIII\"]\n  }\n}\n\nShould I include model_level \"series\"? It duplicates attributes in models. Fine to include or skip; I'll include enclosure_material and load_cell_connection in model_level; series in model attributes only.\n\nDisplay diagonal: \"2.0\\\" or 1.0\\\"\" — the mapping is per model but unknown. I'll set type_level display_size as {\"value\": \"2.0 or 1.0\", \"unit_symbol\": \"in\"}. Hmm \"in\" unit symbol. Acceptable.\n\nAlso note fragment says \"conformity basis: Testing and examination described in Evaluation Report P00917 (13 pages)\". role: type_evaluation_report fits.\n\nLabel for models: omit label (null) or give like \"A-Series indicator AFS\". I'll omit label key? Schema shows label; omit if not present—fine.\n\nfamily_name: \"A-Series and V-Series digital indicators\" — is that an explicit family name? It's a description; maybe null is safer. Rule: explicit family name if any, else null. There's no explicit \"family name\". I'll set null.\n\nLoad cell component: role \"load cell\", alternatives \"OR\" (any compatible load cell). characteristics: {\"requirement\": {\"value\": \"R60 OIML Certificate of Conformity and compatibility of modules data\"}}. Also note \"NH-marked cells only allowed with R76 humidity testing\" already in config_level. Also \"transmission conforms to a standard type\".\n\nA/D conversion module and main board: include as components with role names.\n\nI think that's good. Keep footnote_markers as empty arrays or omit? Schema shape shows footnote_markers[]; I'll include empty arrays consistently in structured values. Actually omitting might be cleaner but the strict shape includes it. I'll include [].\n\nFor string values, unit_symbol null, unit_id null.\n\nDouble-check model mapping:\nA-Series: AFS, AFM, ABM, ATM, APS — stainless steel: AFS, APS; plastic: AFM, ATM, ABM. 4-wire.\nV-Series: VFS, VFM, VBM, VTM, VPS — stainless: VFS, VPS; plastic: VFM, VBM, VTM. 6-wire.\n\nWait plastic list: \"plastic enclosures (AFM, ATM, ABM, VFM, VBM, VTM)\" — yes matches.\n\nOutput single JSON, no fences.",
